Support  for checksum offload is unimplemented.  Particularly for
Yukon‐II hardware,  there  are  multiple  different  receive  and
transmit  offload  silicon bugs which have to be worked around in
software when using hardware offloading.  For this  reason,  sup‐
port for hardware offloading is not very desirable for these con‐
trollers,  and unlikely to be ever implemented.  Performance with
at least some  Marvell‐based  adapters  is  poor,  especially  on
loaded PCI buses or when the adapters are behind PCI‐PCI bridges.
It  is  believed that this is because the Marvell parts have sig‐
nificantly less buffering than the original SysKonnect cards had.
